// C=αop(A)op(B)T+βC
// where α and β are scalars, C is a symmetric matrix stored in lower or upper mode, and A and B are matrices with dimensions op(A)n×k and op(B)n×k , respectively. Also, for matrices A and B
// op(A) and op(B)={A and Bif trans == CUBLAS_OP_NAT and BTif trans == [OpT]
// This routine can be used when B is in such way that the result is guaranteed to be symmetric. A usual example is when the matrix B is a scaled form of the matrix A: this is equivalent to B being the product of the matrix A and a diagonal matrix. For an efficient computation of the product of a regular matrix with a diagonal matrix, refer to the routine cublasdgmm().
// The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below.
// For references please refer to NETLIB documentation:
// ssyrk(), dsyrk(), csyrk(), zsyrk() and
// ssyr2k(), dsyr2k(), csyr2k(), zsyr2k()
//
//   - uplo: Indicates if matrix C lower or upper part, is stored, the other symmetric part is not referenced and is inferred from the stored elements
//   - trans: Operation op( A) that is non- or transpose
//   - n: Number of rows of matrix op( A), op( B) and C
//   - k: Number of columns of matrix op( A) and op( B)
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication
//   - A: < type > array of dimension lda x k with lda >= max(1, n) if transa == [OpN] and lda x n with lda >= max(1, k) otherwise
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - B: < type > array of dimensions ldb x k with ldb >= max(1, n) if transb == [OpN] and ldb x n with ldb >= max(1,k) otherwise
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix B
//   - beta: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If beta == 0, then C does not have to be a valid input
//   - C: < type > array of dimensions ldc x n with ldc >= max(1, n)
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix C
//
// Returns:
//   - [ErrExecutionFailed]: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: - If n < 0 or k < 0, or - if trans is not one of [OpN], [OpT] and [OpC], or - if uplo is not one of [FillModeLower] and [FillModeUpper], or - if lda < max(1, n) when trans == [OpN], and lda < max(1, k) otherwise, or - if ldb < max(1, n) when trans == [OpN], and ldb < max(1, k) otherwise, or - if ldc < max(1, n), or - if alpha or beta are NULL, or - if C is NULL when beta is not zero
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized
//   - [Success]: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasCsyrkx.
func (h Handle) Csyrkx(uplo FillMode, trans Operation, n int32, k int32, alpha *Complex64, A *Complex64, lda int32, B *Complex64, ldb int32, beta *Complex64, C *Complex64, ldc int32) error {
	return csyrkx(h, uplo, trans, n, k, alpha, A, lda, B, ldb, beta, C, ldc)
}

