//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: m < 0, n < 0, or batchCount < 0
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized
//   - [Success]: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasTSTgemvStridedBatched.
func (h Handle) TSTgemvStridedBatched(trans Operation, m int32, n int32, alpha *float32, A *BFloat16, lda int32, strideA int64, x *BFloat16, incx int32, stridex int64, beta *float32, y *BFloat16, incy int32, stridey int64, batchCount int32) error {
	return tSTgemvStridedBatched(h, trans, m, n, alpha, A, lda, strideA, x, incx, stridex, beta, y, incy, stridey, batchCount)
}

// TSTgemvStridedBatched64 supports the 64-bit Integer Interface.
//
// This function performs the matrix-vector multiplication of a batch of matrices and vectors. The batch is considered to be “uniform”, i.e. all instances have the same dimensions (m, n), leading dimension (lda), increments (incx, incy) and transposition (trans) for their respective A matrix, x and y vectors. Input matrix A and vector x, and output vector y for each instance of the batch are located at fixed offsets in number of elements from their locations in the previous instance. Pointers to A matrix, x and y vectors for the first instance are passed to the function by the user along with offsets in number of elements - strideA, stridex and stridey that determine the locations of input matrices and vectors, and output vectors in future instances.
// y+i∗stridey=αop(A+i∗strideA)(x+i∗stridex)+β(y+i∗stridey), for i ∈[0,batchCount−1]
// where α and β are scalars, and A is an array of pointers to matrix stored in column-major format with dimension A [i]m×n , and x and y are arrays of pointers to vectors. Also, for matrix A [i]
// op(A [i])={A [i]if trans == CUBLAS_OP_NA [i]Tif trans == CUBLAS_OP_TA [i]Hif trans == [OpC]
// Note
// y [i] matrices must not overlap, i.e. the individual gemv operations must be computable independently; otherwise, undefined behavior is expected.
// On certain problem sizes, it might be advantageous to make multiple calls to cublasgemv() in different CUDA streams, rather than use this API.
// Note
// In the table below, we use A [i], x [i], y [i] as notation for A matrix, and x and y vectors in the ith instance of the batch, implicitly assuming they are respectively offsets in number of elements strideA, stridex, stridey away from A [i-1], x [i-1], y [i-1]. The unit for the offset is number of elements and must not be zero .
// The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below.
//
//   - trans: Operation op( A [i]) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix A [i]
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix A [i]
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication
//   - A: < type >* pointer to the A matrix corresponding to the first instance of the batch, with dimensions lda x n with lda >= max(1, m)
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store each matrix A [i]
//   - strideA: Value of type long long int that gives the offset in number of elements between A [i] and A [i+1]
//   - x: < type >* pointer to the x vector corresponding to the first instance of the batch, with each dimension n if trans == [OpN] and m otherwise
//   - incx: Stride of each one-dimensional array x [i]
//   - stridex: Value of type long long int that gives the offset in number of elements between x [i] and x [i+1]
//   - beta: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If beta == 0, y does not have to be a valid input
//   - y: < type >* pointer to the y vector corresponding to the first instance of the batch, with each dimension m if trans == [OpN] and n otherwise. Vectors y [i] should not overlap; otherwise, undefined behavior is expected
//   - incy: Stride of each one-dimensional array y [i]
//   - stridey: Value of type long long int that gives the offset in number of elements between y [i] and y [i+1]
//   - batchCount: Number of GEMVs to perform in the batch
//
// Returns:
//   - [ErrExecutionFailed]: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: m < 0, n < 0, or batchCount < 0
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized
//   - [Success]: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasTSTgemvStridedBatched_64.
func (h Handle) TSTgemvStridedBatched64(trans Operation, m int64, n int64, alpha *float32, A *BFloat16, lda int64, strideA int64, x *BFloat16, incx int64, stridex int64, beta *float32, y *BFloat16, incy int64, stridey int64, batchCount int64) error {
	return tSTgemvStridedBatched64(h, trans, m, n, alpha, A, lda, strideA, x, incx, stridex, beta, y, incy, stridey, batchCount)
}

