// Zgbmv supports the 64-bit Integer Interface.
//
// This function performs the banded matrix-vector multiplication
// y=α op(A)x+βy
// where A is a banded matrix with kl subdiagonals and ku superdiagonals, x and y are vectors, and α and β are scalars. Also, for matrix A
// op(A)={A if trans == CUBLAS_OP_NAT if trans == CUBLAS_OP_TAH if trans == [OpC]
// The banded matrix A is stored column by column, with the main diagonal stored in row ku+1 (starting in first position), the first superdiagonal stored in row ku (starting in second position), the first subdiagonal stored in row ku+2 (starting in first position), etc. So that in general, the element A(i,j) is stored in the memory location A(ku+1+i-j,j) for j=1,…,n and i∈[max(1,j−ku),min(m,j+kl)] . Also, the elements in the array A that do not conceptually correspond to the elements in the banded matrix (the top left ku×ku and bottom right kl×kl triangles) are not referenced.
// The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below.
// For references please refer to NETLIB documentation:
// sgbmv(), dgbmv(), cgbmv(), zgbmv()
//
//   - trans: Operation op( A) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix A
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix A
//   - kl: Number of subdiagonals of matrix A
//   - ku: Number of superdiagonals of matrix A
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication
//   - A: < type > array of dimension lda x n with lda >= kl + ku + 1
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - x: < type > vector with n elements if trans == [OpN] and m elements otherwise
//   - incx: Stride between consecutive elements of x
//   - beta: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If beta == 0 then y does not have to be a valid input
//   - y: < type > vector with m elements if trans == [OpN] and n elements otherwise
//   - incy: Stride between consecutive elements of y
//
// Returns:
//   - [ErrExecutionFailed]: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: - If m < 0, n < 0, kl < 0 or ku < 0, or - if lda < (kl + ku + 1), or - if incx == 0 or incy == 0, or - if trans is not one of [OpN], [OpT], [OpC], or - if alpha or beta are NULL
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized
//   - [Success]: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasZgbmv_v2.
func (h Handle) Zgbmv(trans Operation, m int32, n int32, kl int32, ku int32, alpha *Complex128, A *Complex128, lda int32, x *Complex128, incx int32, beta *Complex128, y *Complex128, incy int32) error {
	return zgbmv(h, trans, m, n, kl, ku, alpha, A, lda, x, incx, beta, y, incy)
}

