// Zgeam supports the 64-bit Integer Interface.
//
// This function performs the matrix-matrix addition/transposition
// C=αop(A)+βop(B)
// where α and β are scalars, and A , B and C are matrices stored in column-major format with dimensions op(A)m×n , op(B)m×n and Cm×n , respectively. Also, for matrix A
// op(A)={Aif transa == CUBLAS_OP_NATif transa == CUBLAS_OP_TAHif transa == [OpC]
// and op(B) is defined similarly for matrix B .
// The operation is out-of-place if C does not overlap A or B.
// The in-place mode supports the following two operations,
// C=α*C+βop(B)
// C=αop(A)+β*C
// For in-place mode, if C == A, ldc == lda and transa == [OpN]. If C === B, ldc == ldb and transb == [OpN]. If the user does not meet above requirements, [ErrInvalidValue] is returned.
// The operation includes the following special cases:
// the user can reset matrix C to zero by setting *alpha = beta = 0.
// the user can transpose matrix A by setting *alpha = 1 and *beta = 0.
// The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below.
//
//   - transa: Operation op( A) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - transb: Operation op( B) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix op( A) and C
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix op( B) and C
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If *alpha == 0, A does not have to be a valid input
//   - A: < type > array of dimensions lda x n with lda >= max(1, m) if transa == [OpN] and lda x m with lda >= max(1, n) otherwise
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store the matrix A
//   - beta: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If *beta == 0, B does not have to be a valid input
//   - B: < type > array of dimension ldb x n with ldb >= max(1, m) if transb == [OpN] and ldb x m with ldb >= max(1,n) otherwise
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix B
//   - C: < type > array of dimensions ldc x n with ldc >= max(1, m)
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of a two-dimensional array used to store the matrix C
//
// Returns:
//   - [ErrExecutionFailed]: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: - If m < 0 or n < 0, or - if transa is not one of [OpN], [OpT] and [OpC], or - if transb is not one of [OpN], [OpT] and [OpC], or - if lda < max(1, m) when transa == [OpN], and lda < max(1, n) otherwise, or - if ldb < max(1, m) if transb == [OpN], and ldb < max(1, n) otherwise, or - if ldc < max(1, m), or - if A == C and `(transa != [OpN])
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized
//   - [Success]: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasZgeam.
func (h Handle) Zgeam(transa Operation, transb Operation, m int32, n int32, alpha *Complex128, A *Complex128, lda int32, beta *Complex128, B *Complex128, ldb int32, C *Complex128, ldc int32) error {
	return zgeam(h, transa, transb, m, n, alpha, A, lda, beta, B, ldb, C, ldc)
}

