// Ztrsv supports the 64-bit Integer Interface.
//
// This function solves the triangular linear system with a single right-hand-side
// op(A)x=b
// where A is a triangular matrix stored in lower or upper mode with or without the main diagonal, and x and b are vectors. Also, for matrix A
// op(A)={Aif transa == CUBLAS_OP_NATif transa == CUBLAS_OP_TAHif transa == [OpC]
// The solution x overwrites the right-hand-sides b on exit.
// No test for singularity or near-singularity is included in this function.
// The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below.
// For references please refer to NETLIB documentation:
// strsv(), dtrsv(), ctrsv(), ztrsv()
//
//   - uplo: Indicates if matrix A lower or upper part is stored, the other part is not referenced and is inferred from the stored elements
//   - trans: Operation op( A) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - diag: Indicates if the elements on the main diagonal of matrix A are unity and should not be accessed
//   - n: Number of rows and columns of matrix A
//   - A: < type > array of dimension lda x n, with lda >= max(1, n)
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - x: < type > vector with n elements
//   - incx: Stride between consecutive elements of x
//
// Returns:
//   - [ErrExecutionFailed]: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: - If n < 0, or - if incx == 0, or - if trans is not one of [OpN], [OpT] and [OpC], or - if uplo is not one of [FillModeLower] and [FillModeUpper], or - if diag is not one of [DiagUnit] and [DiagNonUnit], or - if lda < max(1, n)
